# Flow-manager browser-turn monitoring (binding)

Canonical contract:
Canonical long-running launcher runbook: [`docs/flow-manager-long-running-child-runbook.md`](../../docs/flow-manager-long-running-child-runbook.md) — use `npm run flow-manager-browser-gpt-long-run` for applicable long turns; the Cursor rule remains a thin pointer.
 [`.claude/skills/create-issue-draft/SKILL.md`](../../.claude/skills/create-issue-draft/SKILL.md) — **Browser-GPT turn transport — Issues #1120 and #1150**.

## One normal monitoring path

For create-issue-draft and pack-review Browser-GPT work, `npm run chatgpt-browser-turn -- turn ...` is the normal low-token fast path and the only routine browser-turn monitor.

- One invocation opens one dedicated owned ChatGPT tab, sends the exact user prompt once, and then observes that same tab until completion or an invocation-local failure.
- Page/DOM completion is sufficient. Do not require service-terminal/network witness fields after the final assistant reply is visibly stable and no longer generating.
- The helper may use bounded low-frequency polling after initial dispatch observation. A normal waiting/generating poll is not an incident.
- A direct helper failure affects only that invocation. It does not authorize a profile-, conversation-, task-, Issue-, PR-, or agent-wide gate.
- Owned-tab cleanup is progressive and local. Never close or commandeer sibling/foreign ChatGPT tabs.

## Configured plural-source launch contract (#1150)

T3 `competitive` and `architectural-review` are each one staggered concurrent batch with one `stageAttemptId` and policy `triple-source/v1`.

`OPK_GPT_REVIEWER_CARDINALITY` is the single operator control. The default T3 cardinality is 3; T1/T2 remain singular. Every stage receipt and invocation envelope freezes the selected `reviewerCardinality` and `cardinalityConfigIdentity`. Required slots are exact `01..N`, not hard-coded `01/02/03`.

- Start all N slots before harvesting or adjudicating any sibling result. Preserve 10–15 second spacing and bounded observation of earlier slots; do not invent an account-wide concurrency cap.
- Every invocation emits one immutable `reviewer-invocation-envelope/v1` bound to `reviewEpisodeId`, `stageAttemptId`, policy, stage, frozen `sourceRevision`, cardinality/config identity, reviewer slot/ordinal, invocation identity, reviewer-source identity, terminal-result identity, revision checks, capacity observation, `send_count`, retry-attempt state, retry class, and terminal classification.
- Successful siblings write separate source-suffixed captures: `pass-NN-competitive-SS.capture.txt` or `pass-NN-architectural-review-SS.capture.txt`. Never consolidate, rewrite, or move sibling captures to satisfy a file-count guard.
- The final `stage-completeness-receipt/v1` is the only persisted stage authority. It belongs to one task-wide no-overwrite receipt sequence with canonical previous links and cumulative census.
- The immutable `tier-intake/v1` task identity plus first frozen revision roots the episode. Guards read every stage receipt in the canonical review directory; a caller-selected subset or later-revision re-root is not authority.
- Episode-wide governed/relayed unions and counts are derived, never persisted as an episode receipt.
- One exact configured-N capture `stageAttemptId` is one logical round. Final T3 activation remains blocked until #1123 replaces Issue-lifetime capture-file counting with logical-round authority.

## Invocation-local retry and settlement

Blind restart is forbidden after any possible or confirmed send.

- One paced retry under the same slot and `stageAttemptId` is permitted only when the terminal helper result proves a pre-send zero-send quota/composer/fill failure and reports `send_count: 0`.
- The retry uses `attemptOrdinal: 2` and `retryAttempt: true`; it consumes the only retry and cannot remain retry-eligible. A failed retry may settle blocked/exhausted.
- A post-send failure, ambiguous delivery, output conflict, missing terminal result, or any result with `send_count: 1` is incident evidence and forbids resend.
- A proven zero-send result with unused retry eligibility keeps the stage attempt unsettled until the retry runs or eligibility is explicitly abandoned and the attempt settles blocked.
- Relay/adjudication begins only after every launched invocation is terminal, no retry runs or remains eligible, and final revision checks match the frozen attempt revision.
- Every partial, blocked, or incident attempt remains ordered evidence. A later stage cannot start before the preceding required stage has credentialed.

## Claude producer evidence

A Claude `architectural-lens` receipt cannot prove its own producer provenance. A counted Claude capture requires a separately produced immutable `claude-producer-evidence/v1` artifact matching episode, attempt, revision, invocation, producing run, terminal result, exit status, M3 status, and capture bytes/hash. A valid unavailable waiver contributes no capture or M3 authority.

## Legacy state is not admission authority

Do **not** gate create/review progress on any of the following:

- `status/list`, `clear`, capability/Gate-B;
- `possible_delivery`, `profile_wall`, stale recovery/orphan records;
- browser/profile/conversation mutexes, claims, queues, leases, or helper-wide blocked state;
- shell PID/log growth as evidence that ChatGPT is still generating.

Legacy control commands may remain available for compatibility/evidence lookup, but they cannot decide whether a new Browser-GPT invocation may start.

## Unexpected events and restart

When the helper directly observes foreign/interleaved user activity, page loss, UI contract failure, cleanup failure, timeout, output conflict, or another unexpected browser-turn event:

1. retain and report the invocation-local terminal result or explicit missing-terminal incident;
2. append the compact event best-effort to `~/.local/state/create-issue-draft/browser-turn-recurrence.jsonl`;
3. include the same direct event in the current flow-manager report;
4. leave sibling Browser-GPT work alone;
5. do not restart unless the result proves an eligible zero-send failure under the rule above.

Duplicate recoverable text is not a reason to reintroduce global recovery/clear machinery. Source-preserving receipts and relay verification govern what may progress.

## Sanctioned one-shot page probe

When direct page diagnosis is genuinely needed, use only the canonical one-shot utility:

```bash
npm run browser-gpt-page-probe -- list --cdp http://127.0.0.1:9222
npm run browser-gpt-page-probe -- inspect --cdp http://127.0.0.1:9222 --target-id <exact-target-id>
npm run browser-gpt-page-probe -- inspect --cdp http://127.0.0.1:9222 --url <exact-conversation-url> --open-if-missing true
npm run browser-gpt-page-probe -- liveness --cdp http://127.0.0.1:9222
```

The exact URL form remains existing-target-only unless `--open-if-missing true` is explicitly supplied. It reuses exactly one normalized match without closing it; with zero matches it may create one page, waits for exact normalized conversation identity and bounded readable SPA state, then closes only the valid target identity returned by that same invocation. A redirect or same-path cross-host result is `surface_unknown` with `conversation_identity_mismatch`. Duplicate matches, malformed creation, cleanup failure, and every reused-page path fail closed without guessed or delayed cleanup.

`liveness` is a single passive census with immediate `MAX_TARGETS` fan-out and independent target deadlines. It reports responsive, unresponsive, or unavailable rows and exact unresponsive IDs; it never creates, closes, navigates, sends, reloads, or infers process death. Every operation runs once and exits with no watch loop, daemon, retry, background owner, or retained state.

The probe is **diagnostic only**:

- `generation_in_progress: false` is not completion evidence;
- node counts, hashes, witnesses, liveness rows, acquisition metadata, and an exported node file do not authorize publication, completion, retry, resend, cleanup, admission, recovery, review capture, or stage progression;
- use inspection output to select exactly one node representation for optional offline export; never request or construct a transcript dump;
- exported text may be sensitive. The caller supplies a new path in an existing directory and owns protection and cleanup of the resulting file.

Do not replace this command with raw CDP WebSocket scripts, Playwright snippets, `salvage-*.mjs`, caller-supplied selectors/JavaScript, a watch loop, or a second supported probe.

## Forbidden duplicate monitoring and authority

- No independent 5–10 or 10–15 minute watchdog layered over the helper.
- No periodic browser-tab sweeper that closes tabs it did not open.
- No reporting "still running" from shell/PID/log state alone.
- No probe-driven takeover, helper bypass, resend, or workflow progression.
- No flow-manager consolidation or content judgment over sibling reviewer output.

The one-shot page probe diagnoses an already-open page, or one explicitly acquired under the zero-match ownership contract; it is not a fallback state machine or browser-turn owner.

## Session handoff

Never end a flow-manager turn with only "background job running". Status must name the owned chat URL when known, the helper result or latest direct observation, the `reviewEpisodeId`/`stageAttemptId`/slot when applicable, any direct incident surfaced by the helper, and the next flow action.